## STAGE 2: INTELLIGENCE

**Trigger:** Stage 1 complete

**Purpose:** Research incumbent contract, pricing history, context for competitive positioning

**Steps:**
```
[2.1] USASpending.gov Search — Incumbent Contract Identification
      ├── Search: Agency + NAICS + "Description of Requirement" keywords
      ├── Identify: Current/previous contract award
      ├── Extract:
      │   ├── Incumbent contractor name
      │   ├── Contract value (awarded amount)
      │   ├── Period of performance
      │   ├── Contract number (PIID)
      │   └── Award date
      └── Save: INCUMBENT_INTELLIGENCE.md

[2.2] FPDS.gov Deep Dive — Contract Details
      ├── Search: PIID from USASpending
      ├── Extract:
      │   ├── Contract modifications (option years exercised?)
      │   ├── Delivery/task orders issued
      │   ├── Pricing structure (fixed price, T&M, etc.)
      │   └── Contracting office contact
      └── Append to INCUMBENT_INTELLIGENCE.md

[2.3] SAM.gov Contract History
      ├── Search for previous solicitations
      ├── Find: Last RFP/RFQ for this requirement
      ├── Extract: Previous pricing if publicly posted
      └── Note: How many bidders last time?

[2.4] Incumbent Strength/Weakness Analysis
      File: COMPETITIVE_INTELLIGENCE.md
      Content:
      ├── Incumbent: [Name]
      ├── Contract Value: [$X]
      ├── Years on Contract: [X]
      ├── Strengths:
      │   ├── [Incumbent advantage 1]
      │   └── [Incumbent advantage 2]
      └── Weaknesses (DDI opportunities):
          ├── [Potential issue 1 — e.g., pricing escalated]
          ├── [Potential issue 2 — e.g., past performance concern]
          └── [How DDI counters each weakness]

[2.5] Pricing Benchmarking
      File: PRICING_INTELLIGENCE.md
      Content:
      ├── Historical Contract Value: [$X over Y years]
      ├── Per-Unit Pricing (if available):
      │   ├── [Item 1]: $[X] per [unit]
      │   └── [Item 2]: $[X] per [unit]
      ├── Labor Rates (if service contract):
      │   ├── [Role 1]: $[X]/hour
      │   └── [Role 2]: $[X]/hour
      ├── DDI Estimated Market Pricing:
      │   ├── [Item 1]: $[X] (based on ThomasNet/distributor research)
      │   └── [Item 2]: $[X]
      ├── Recommended DDI Bid Pricing:
      │   ├── [With X% margin]: $[X]
      │   └── [Competitive positioning]: Match/Beat/Strategic premium
      └── Pricing Strategy Notes:

[2.6] Win Strategy Development
      File: WIN_STRATEGY.md
      Content:
      ├── Why DDI Wins:
      │   ├── EDWOSB advantage (if set-aside)
      │   ├── [Specific differentiator 1]
      │   └── [Specific differentiator 2]
      ├── Proposal Themes:
      │   ├── Theme 1: [e.g., "Proven Local Performance"]
      │   ├── Theme 2: [e.g., "EDWOSB Socioeconomic Value"]
      │   └── Theme 3: [e.g., "Superior Service Model"]
      ├── Risk Mitigation:
      │   ├── [Risk 1] → [Mitigation strategy]
      │   └── [Risk 2] → [Mitigation strategy]
      └── Competitive Positioning:
          ├── vs. Incumbent: [Strategy]
          └── vs. Other new bidders: [Strategy]

[2.7] Stage 2 complete → Advance to Stage 3
```

**Status File Updates:**
- WORKFLOW_CHECKLIST.md: Step 3 [✓] (subs sourcing triggered), Step 4 [ ]
- Airtable: Source Status = "Stage 2: Intelligence Complete — Incumbent & pricing research done"

**What Dee Sees:**
```
📊 INCUMBENT_INTELLIGENCE.md — Complete
📊 COMPETITIVE_INTELLIGENCE.md — Complete
📊 PRICING_INTELLIGENCE.md — Complete
📊 WIN_STRATEGY.md — Complete

💡 Key Insight: [Example] "Incumbent [Name] at $450K/year. DDI can deliver at $380K with 25% margin."

⏭️ Stage 3 — Subcontractor/Supplier Resourcing
```

