## STAGE 3: RESOURCING

**Trigger:** Stage 2 complete (intelligence gathered, pricing strategy set)

**Purpose:** Secure the team (subs) and supply chain (suppliers) to deliver

**Steps:**

### For Service Contracts:
```
[3.1] Subcontractor Database Search
      Query Airtable SUBCONTRACTORS table:
      ├── Service match: [drug testing/fingerprinting/grounds/etc.]
      ├── Location match: [opportunity state/region]
      ├── Status: Active, vetted
      └── Insurance: Current
      Result: [X] Tier 1 (existing vetted) subs identified

[3.2] Web Research for New Subcontractors
      ├── Search: "[service] providers [city/state]"
      ├── Industry directories (eScreen, SWFT, etc.)
      └── Compile: Tier 2 candidate list
      Result: [X] Tier 2 candidates identified

[3.3] USASpending Competition Check (MANDATORY)
      For EACH candidate (Tier 1 and Tier 2):
      ├── Search usaspending.gov for legal company name
      ├── CHECK: Do they win their own gov contracts?
      │   ├── YES → CROSS OFF (they're competition, not partner)
      │   └── NO → KEEP (ideal sub — registered but needs prime)
      └── Document: SUBCONTRACTOR_PROSPECTS.md

[3.4] Subcontractor Vetting (6-Pillar Framework)
      File: SUBCONTRACTOR_VETTING_CHECKLIST.md
      For each candidate:
      ├── PILLAR 1: VET — Qualifications, references, SAM status
      ├── PILLAR 2: PROTECT — NDA, Non-Compete
      ├── PILLAR 3: INSURE — COI verification
      ├── PILLAR 4: PLAN — Staffing & work plan
      ├── PILLAR 5: COMMUNICATE — Reporting cadence
      └── PILLAR 6: MANAGE — Performance metrics

[3.5] Subcontractor Outreach
      Generate:
      ├── SUBCONTRACTOR_OUTREACH_EMAIL.md (generic scope)
      ├── SUBCONTRACTOR_SCOPE.md (safe-to-share deliverables)
      └── COI_REQUEST_EMAIL.md

[3.6] Subcontractor Selection
      ├── Select best qualified sub
      ├── Negotiate pricing (internal, not client-facing)
      └── Lock in commitment

[3.7] Update Pricing with Sub Costs
      File: PRICING_WORKSHEET.md
      ├── Sub Cost: $[X]
      ├── DDI Management Fee: $[Y] (% or fixed)
      ├── Total Cost to DDI: $[X+Y]
      ├── DDI Bid Price to Govt: $[Z] (from Stage 2 strategy)
      ├── DDI Margin: $[Z - (X+Y)] ([X]%)
      └── Margin Check: ≥15%? If no, flag for review.
```

### For Product Contracts:
```
[3.1] Supplier Sourcing Guide
      File: SUPPLIER_SOURCING_GUIDE.md
      Content:
      ├── Product specifications from solicitation
      ├── Search terms for ThomasNet/Manta
      ├── Authorized distributor requirements
      └── Geographic sourcing strategy

[3.2] RFQ Generation (if not done in Stage 1)
      File: DDI-2026-###_RFQ_[Product].pdf
      ├── Buyer protection applied (NO buyer names)
      ├── DDI-YYYY-### numbering
      ├── Deadline: Govt deadline - 5 days
      └── Specifications table

[3.3] Supplier Outreach
      ├── Email RFQ to 3-5 suppliers
      ├── Track responses in Airtable
      └── Follow-up at 48hrs, 72hrs if no response

[3.4] Quote Collection & Analysis
      File: SUPPLIER_QUOTES_ANALYSIS.md
      ├── Supplier 1: $[X] | Terms: [Net 30/etc] | Lead time: [X days]
      ├── Supplier 2: $[Y] | Terms: [ ] | Lead time: [ ]
      ├── Supplier 3: $[Z] | Terms: [ ] | Lead time: [ ]
      └── Recommendation: [Best value selection]

[3.5] Pricing Calculation
      File: PRICING_WORKSHEET.md
      ├── Supplier Cost: $[X]
      ├── Freight/Shipping: $[Y]
      ├── Insurance/Bonding (if required): $[Z]
      ├── DDI Management Fee: $[A]
      ├── Total Cost: $[X+Y+Z+A]
      ├── DDI Bid Price to Govt: $[B] (from Stage 2 strategy)
      ├── DDI Margin: $[B - Total Cost] ([X]%)
      └── Margin Check: ≥15%? If no, flag for review.
```

**Status File Updates:**
- WORKFLOW_CHECKLIST.md: Step 3 [✓], Step 4 [✓], Step 5 [✓], Step 6 [✓], Step 7 [✓], Step 8 [ ]
- Airtable: Source Status = "Stage 3: Resourcing Complete — Team & supply chain secured"

